`255`, `256` (the size\n  `doubleneg` hard-codes), `>256`.\n* match position: first / middle / last / absent / duplicated (`memchr` returns\n  the *first*).\n* `search_val` byte domain: `0x00`, `0x2A` (the literal `42` at `lib.c:106`),\n  `0x7F`, `0x80`, `0xFF`, plus values needing `& 0xFF` narrowing.\n* `int` sign/magnitude classes: `0`, `1`, `-1`, small +/-, `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`.\n* `b == 0` vs `b != 0` (`lib.c:57`).\n* `c % 10` ∈ `-9..=9` — 19 distinct `pow` exponents (`lib.c:61`).\n* zero/non-zero pattern of `doubleneg`'s four params: full 2^4 = 16 truth table\n  (each param feeds a distinct `!!` at `lib.c:76,81,82,83`).\n\n## Configuration rows\n\nEvery row is exercised with **many randomized inputs** from a fixed-seed\nSplitMix64 generator (reproducible) in `tests/phase_b_valid.rs` /\n`tests/phase_b_doubleneg.rs`, comparing the C `.so` and Rust `.so` byte-for-byte\nvia `libloading`.\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|----|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1  | `convert_double_to_int` | in-range exact integers, both signs, incl. `0.0` / `-0.0` | [x] |\n| 2  | `convert_double_to_int` | in-range fractional values → truncation **toward zero** (not floor) for positive and negative | [x] |\n| 3  | `convert_double_to_int` | subnormal / tiny magnitudes (`±5e-324`, `±1e-300`) → `0` | [x] |\n| 4  | `convert_double_to_int` | at the `int` boundary: `±2147483647.x`, `-2147483648.0`, `2147483647.9999999` | [x] |\n| 5  | `convert_double_to_int` | randomized full-domain `f64` bit patterns (all classes mixed, incl. inf/NaN) | [x] |\n| 6  | `find_value_in_buffer` | `size=1`, byte present (match at index 0 = last = only) | [x] |\n| 7  | `find_value_in_buffer` | `size=2`, match at index 0 vs index 1 (first-match precedence) | [x] |\n| 8  | `find_value_in_buffer` | `size=256`, match at first / middle / last index | [x] |\n| 9  | `find_value_in_buffer` | duplicated target → must return the **lowest** index | [x] |\n| 10 | `find_value_in_buffer` | target is `0x00` inside a buffer that also contains later `0x00`s | [x] |\n| 11 | `find_value_in_buffer` | target `0x80`/`0xFF` (high-bit bytes) through the signed-`char` cast | [x] |\n| 12 | `find_value_in_buffer` | `size` smaller than the buffer, with the only match **beyond** `size` | [x] |\n| 13 | `find_value_in_buffer` | randomized buffers (lengths `1..=512`) × randomized `search_val` over the full `int` domain | [x] |\n| 14 | `process_negation` | `0`, `1`, `-1`, `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`, `256`, `0x10000` (low bits zero) | [x] |\n| 15 | `process_negation` | randomized full `int` domain | [x] |\n| 16 | `create_numeric_buffer` | `size=1` — single element, seed `0` | [x] |\n| 17 | `create_numeric_buffer` | `size=7` (equals the stride) — verifies the `i*7` progression | [x] |\n| 18 | `create_numeric_buffer` | `size=256` — one full permutation of all byte values (`gcd(7,256)=1`) | [x] |\n| 19 | `create_numeric_buffer` | `size=512` — two wraps of the `% 256` cycle | [x] |\n| 20 | `create_numeric_buffer` | `size < capacity` — writes exactly `size` bytes, leaves the tail untouched | [x] |\n| 21 | `create_numeric_buffer` | negative seeds → negative C remainder → negative `char` | [x] |\n| 22 | `create_numeric_buffer` | `seed` near `INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN` so `seed + i*7` wraps mid-loop | [x] |\n| 23 | `create_numeric_buffer` | randomized `(size, seed)`, full byte-array comparison | [x] |\n| 24 | `calculate_with_doubles` | `b != 0`, exact division (`a` a multiple of `b`), `c % 10 == 0` → `pow(10,0)` | [x] |\n| 25 | `calculate_with_doubles` | `b != 0`, inexact division → full `f64` rounding must match bit-for-bit | [x] |\n| 26 | `calculate_with_doubles` | `b == 0` guard taken (`result` stays `0.0`), swept over all `c % 10` | [x] |\n| 27 | `calculate_with_doubles` | all 19 distinct exponents `c % 10 ∈ -9..=9`, `a`/`b` fixed | [x] |\n| 28 | `calculate_with_doubles` | all four sign combinations of `(a, b)`, incl. `a == 0` | [x] |\n| 29 | 